  "limitations": [
    "Acceptance uses migrated/seeded file-backed SQLite and local in-process ASGI/runtime composition with deterministic mock adapters. No live provider, PostgreSQL concurrency, OS-kill or deployment claim is made.",
    "Observers invoke the real provider delegates. Failure seams inject unexpected dispatcher exceptions before provider entry or raise only after the original audit append flushes; no positive response, persisted authority or audit row is manufactured.",
    "Composed journeys cover completed READ/Email, approval rejection/renewal, cancellation and unexpected worker failure. Existing lifecycle, approval, audit contract, concurrency, redaction and public API gates supplement these concrete paths; this is not an exhaustive enumeration of every possible workflow interleaving.",
    "Clock-based metadata expiry proves public projection suppression while retaining the complete event skeleton. It does not claim a physical retention sweep or cryptographic tamper-proof storage; direct local database administration remains a residual risk.",
    "Only the global audit feed promises a fixed pagination high watermark. Run timeline pages use monotonic run sequences. Shared acceptance helpers are reused from previously verified requirement tests.",
    "All pytest gates deny Python sockets except local Unix sockets. No server or child browser is launched. CI remains disabled; no CI or network-isolated subprocess guarantee is inferred."
  ]
